.\" Manual page for rdpd(8).  mdoc format.
.Dd May 25, 2026
.Dt RDPD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rdpd
.Nd Remote Desktop Protocol server
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl AdfPVW
.Op Fl h Ar host
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Op Fl S Ar socket
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the Remote Desktop Protocol server.  It listens for incoming RDP
connections, presents a graphical login screen drawn directly with
RDP drawing orders, authenticates the user via
.Xr rdp-sessionmgr 8 ,
and spawns a fresh per-user X11 session.  The server speaks RDP
natively; there is no VNC in the stack.
.Pp
The daemon implements the full RDP handshake (TPKT, X.224, TLS, MCS,
license, capability negotiation, finalization) and supports
Network Level Authentication
.Pq NLA
via the
.Sy PROTOCOL_HYBRID
security mode (CredSSP with NTLMv2).
Clients negotiating NLA are authenticated before any session is created.
.Pp
Graphical output is sent as H.264 / AVC420 frames over the
.Sy RDPGFX
(Graphics Pipeline) dynamic virtual channel when the client supports
it, falling back to fast-path bitmap updates otherwise.
A bitmap update too large for a single fast-path PDU is split into
FIRST/NEXT/LAST fragments sized to the client's MultifragmentUpdate
MaxRequestSize (a 16KB safe default is used when the client omits it),
while small updates remain single-fragment.
Audio from the session is forwarded to the client via the
.Sy RDPSND
channel (PCM 16-bit stereo, 44.1 kHz).
Client drive, printer, and serial device redirection is handled by the
.Sy RDPDR
channel.
Multi-monitor layouts are parsed from the GCC CS_MONITOR block, and
dynamic resize is supported over the RDPEDISP Display Control channel,
which the server opens and on which it advertises its monitor limits.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl A
Enable auto-login mode.  Credentials from the Client Info PDU are
used directly for authentication; the built-in greeter is skipped.
.It Fl d
Enable debug logging.
.It Fl f
Run in the foreground and log to standard error instead of
.Xr syslog 3 .
.It Fl h Ar host
Bind to
.Ar host
instead of all addresses.
.It Fl p Ar port
Listen on
.Ar port
instead of 3389.
.It Fl S Ar socket
Path to the
.Xr rdp-sessionmgr 8
AF_UNIX socket.
When omitted, the built-in stub authenticator accepts any non-empty
username/password pair.
.It Fl V
Offer RDPGFX AVC
.Pq H.264
graphics to v10.x clients
.Pq mstsc , macOS
that advertise it by omitting the
.Sy AVC_DISABLED
capability flag.
This is off by default: a client may advertise AVC yet be unable to
decode it
.Pq for example a Microsoft client on a host without a GPU ,
in which case it tears down the graphics channel instead of falling
back, ending the session.
.Xr xfreerdp 1 ,
which advertises the v8.1
.Sy AVC420_ENABLED
flag, is always offered AVC regardless of this option.
.It Fl P
Offer RFX Progressive
.Pq MS-RDPEGFX RFX_PROGRESSIVE
graphics to GFX-capable clients that are not given AVC.
Unlike AVC, it is a CPU-decodable wavelet codec that needs no client
GPU, so it accelerates GPU-less clients
.Pq mstsc , macOS , Android
without the AVC teardown described above.
Off by default; the per-frame codec is selected by the WireToSurface2
command, so it does not affect clients that receive AVC.
.It Fl W
Prefer G.711 A-law audio output when the client supports it.
A-law is half the wire bandwidth of 16-bit PCM at a small quality cost,
so it suits WAN links.
Off by default; PCM is used on a LAN.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/rdpd.conf
Configuration file (see
.Xr rdpd.conf 5 ;
not yet honoured).
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr rdpd.conf 5 ,
.Xr rdp-sessionmgr 8 ,
.Xr rdp-session 8
